msgid "Using SSL with native executables"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We are quickly moving to an SSL-everywhere world so being able to use SSL is "
"crucial."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Since GraalVM 21.3, TLS works in native executables out of the box: the JDK "
"TLS stack\n"
"is included automatically, so TLS on the HTTP server and on most clients "
"requires no\n"
"extra configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The exception is clients that go through the `java.net.URL` / "
"`HttpsURLConnection`\n"
"`https` protocol handler, such as the REST client used in this guide. That "
"handler must\n"
"be enabled explicitly when building the native executable, which is what\n"
"`quarkus.ssl.native` (and the underlying `-H:EnableURLProtocols=https` "
"option) controls.\n"
"This guide walks through that mechanism, and through configuring the trust "
"store used at\n"
"run time."
msgstr ""

